WEBVTT

00:00:10.500 --> 00:00:20.170
<b>LEGEND</b>

00:00:10.500 --> 00:00:20.170
<b>OF THE</b>

00:00:10.500 --> 00:00:20.170
<b>  GALACTIC HEROES</b>

00:01:42.970 --> 00:01:47.320
The history of
Goldenbaum's Galactic Empire...

00:01:47.320 --> 00:01:51.800
...is filled with victory and
defeat, honor and dishonor.

00:01:53.050 --> 00:02:01.720
Among the less than glorious records are
the losses at the Battle of Dagon in 331...

00:02:03.520 --> 00:02:07.130
...and at Shandaruwa in 387.

00:02:08.730 --> 00:02:12.690
The rebellion of the soldiers
under Admiral Teleman in 408.

00:02:13.470 --> 00:02:17.270
The defection{exile} of Admiral
Seigmeister in 419.

00:02:17.950 --> 00:02:20.630
The loss in Holzetti
Starzone that same year.

00:02:21.550 --> 00:02:26.450
The assassination of
Admiral Michaelsen in 442.

00:02:26.990 --> 00:02:32.650
But the loss in the Battle of the Arlesheim
Starzone in 483 was equally devastating.

00:02:38.580 --> 00:02:43.720
Vice Admiral Keyserling's fleet
detected movement from the Alliance...

00:02:43.720 --> 00:02:46.990
...and was planning a
timely surprise attack.

00:02:49.000 --> 00:02:51.720
But before the time came...

00:02:51.720 --> 00:02:55.300
...the Imperial fleet opened fire against the Admiral's orders.

00:03:04.340 --> 00:03:06.920
As a result of the Alliance's counterattack...

00:03:06.920 --> 00:03:12.500
...the Imperial fleet suffered a decisive
loss and was completely routed.

00:03:15.880 --> 00:03:21.200
The outcome was predictable, as the
fleet gave up the element of surprise...

00:03:21.200 --> 00:03:23.320
...by opening fire in the
midst of the enemy fleet.

00:03:25.070 --> 00:03:28.000
The mortality rate of the
Keyserling Fleet was more than 60%.

00:03:29.720 --> 00:03:39.890
This decisive defeat, as a result of this failure, severely damaged the pride of the Imperial forces.

00:03:43.530 --> 00:03:48.950
When Keyserling returned home with his
defeated troops, a court martial awaited him.

00:03:49.830 --> 00:03:57.350
He was blamed for incompetence,
especially his inability to lead his soldiers.

00:03:58.430 --> 00:04:01.720
He was deemed responsible
for the untimely attack...

00:04:01.720 --> 00:04:07.740
...that gave away the element of surprise,
and the subsequent debacle that followed.

00:04:10.190 --> 00:04:15.170
Because of Kaiser Friedrich IV's
illness, he was pardoned.

00:04:15.170 --> 00:04:19.170
Keyserling was demoted to
Rear Admiral and then discharged.

00:04:19.170 --> 00:04:26.130
But Keyserling's reputation was irretrievably damaged due to his obstinate silence at his court martial.

00:04:30.130 --> 00:04:37.220
Dishonor

00:04:30.130 --> 00:04:37.220
Chapter 1

00:04:50.000 --> 00:04:52.420
Attention, all passengers.

00:04:54.310 --> 00:05:00.830
We will soon arrive at Kreuznach III,
a satellite of the Planet Zoft.

00:05:02.320 --> 00:05:07.420
At Kreuznach III, many leisure and
amusement facilities are at your disposal...

00:05:07.420 --> 00:05:11.900
...for an enjoyable vacation.

00:05:13.370 --> 00:05:18.110
For those passengers that are scheduled
to make a stop, please be reminded...

00:05:18.320 --> 00:05:19.490
Vacation...

00:05:25.530 --> 00:05:28.030
So you won't be coming ?

00:05:28.580 --> 00:05:31.160
No, I'll be about
three days late.

00:05:31.430 --> 00:05:35.280
You should go ahead and depart,
according to our initial plan.

00:05:35.280 --> 00:05:40.630
I would rather wait on
Odin and accompany you.

00:05:40.630 --> 00:05:44.170
Also, we must prepare for the
expedition early next year.

00:05:44.170 --> 00:05:47.320
The preparations have already
been under way for some time.

00:05:47.320 --> 00:05:50.680
But we know the admirals
assigned to this expedition...

00:05:50.680 --> 00:05:54.560
...aren't too enthusiastic about
being under your command.

00:05:54.560 --> 00:06:00.090
You mean Merkatz, Staden, Forgel,
Fahrenheit and Erlache...

00:06:00.090 --> 00:06:03.830
They're civilized, so
they won't rebel openly...

00:06:03.830 --> 00:06:07.080
...but the expedition will be difficult if
they only pretend to follow your orders.

00:06:07.920 --> 00:06:12.220
Once on the battlefield, they'll have
no choice but to follow my orders.

00:06:12.220 --> 00:06:13.970
I'm sure they will.

00:06:13.970 --> 00:06:15.260
Don't worry.

00:06:15.260 --> 00:06:19.390
Besides, we can't do anything
about it for the time being.

00:06:19.390 --> 00:06:21.450
You're right.

00:06:21.450 --> 00:06:23.560
By the way, what was the urgent
business you talked about ?

00:06:23.560 --> 00:06:27.120
It's been decided that I am
to be given the title of Count.

00:06:27.120 --> 00:06:30.380
Next year, when I am
promoted to High Admiral...

00:06:30.380 --> 00:06:34.260
...I will also become
Count Reinhard von Lohengramm.

00:06:35.000 --> 00:06:39.390
I will have to visit the graves of the
original Lohengramms and what-not.

00:06:40.240 --> 00:06:42.950
You will not be using the
surname Musel any longer ?

00:06:42.950 --> 00:06:43.770
Musel ?!

00:06:43.770 --> 00:06:48.080
Musel is the surname of a man who sold his daughter to the Kaiser !

00:06:48.080 --> 00:06:49.900
I have no emotional
attachment to it !

00:06:50.420 --> 00:06:51.540
Lord Reinhard...

00:06:52.890 --> 00:06:56.490
There are still things
I don't understand about him.

00:06:57.540 --> 00:07:01.320
The Lohengramms were a family of
distinction from the founding of this nation.

00:07:01.320 --> 00:07:04.190
That means they've oppressed the
people, persecuted activists...

00:07:04.190 --> 00:07:11.320
...killed unarmed women and children,
and imprisoned political offenders.

00:07:11.320 --> 00:07:16.120
But I like the sound of the name
Lohengramm much better than Musel.

00:07:17.790 --> 00:07:19.060
That's the story.

00:07:19.060 --> 00:07:21.580
Once in a while, you should
enjoy a vacation without me.

00:07:21.580 --> 00:07:23.790
It's only two or three days.

00:07:23.790 --> 00:07:29.070
Besides, if I make you work too
hard, my sister will scold me.

00:07:30.260 --> 00:07:32.340
Then I will do
as you tell me.

00:09:22.690 --> 00:09:23.540
Come in, come in.

00:09:25.220 --> 00:09:26.370
It's cheap.

00:09:26.370 --> 00:09:27.830
You won't regret it.

00:09:30.720 --> 00:09:32.170
Have you decided
where you'll be staying ?

00:09:32.170 --> 00:09:33.940
We've got nice rooms here.

00:09:33.940 --> 00:09:37.380
Hello there, won't you
come in for a drink ?

00:09:37.380 --> 00:09:39.050
I'll give you a discount.

00:09:40.050 --> 00:09:43.850
If you want to get rich,
come to Kasino Schwartzstein.

00:09:43.850 --> 00:09:45.620
Try your luck,
try your luck !

00:09:47.260 --> 00:09:49.490
Hello, handsome.

00:09:49.490 --> 00:09:50.910
Won't you come in and play ?

00:09:52.750 --> 00:09:53.670
Woof !

00:09:57.020 --> 00:09:57.730
Hi.

00:09:57.730 --> 00:10:01.100
The famous Kreuznach Dog Races
will start soon, just around the corner.

00:10:06.100 --> 00:10:07.030
Hello, Mister.

00:10:07.030 --> 00:10:08.490
You have a nice body.

00:10:08.490 --> 00:10:10.080
Do you want to
play some sports ?

00:10:10.080 --> 00:10:12.350
We've rented a
flying ball court over there.

00:10:13.650 --> 00:10:15.120
There's a sale on !
It's cheap !

00:10:15.120 --> 00:10:17.580
Genuine brand name stuff !

00:10:17.580 --> 00:10:19.540
It's genuine and cheap !

00:10:20.520 --> 00:10:23.080
This sort of place doesn't
really suit my tastes.

00:10:24.120 --> 00:10:26.910
I can't enjoy myself when
and where I'm supposed to.

00:10:26.910 --> 00:10:29.070
I guess that's an unfortunate
part of who I am.

00:10:44.730 --> 00:10:50.620
Imperial Fleet Commander Siegfried
Kircheis, on a five day vacation.

00:10:54.010 --> 00:10:57.580
I beg your pardon, but for a
Commander, you seem very young.

00:10:59.070 --> 00:11:00.070
I've been told that before.

00:11:02.390 --> 00:11:03.570
I can't blame him.

00:11:03.570 --> 00:11:05.720
For someone from an aristocratic family,
such advancement may be plausible...

00:11:05.720 --> 00:11:08.520
...but it's highly unusual for a
commoner like myself, after all.

00:11:08.520 --> 00:11:11.720
If I told him that I'll soon become
a Captain, I wonder what he'd say.

00:11:13.190 --> 00:11:15.420
It's room 1204.

00:11:15.420 --> 00:11:16.510
Have a nice stay.

00:11:17.020 --> 00:11:18.410
Thank you.

00:12:48.050 --> 00:12:51.380
It seems you saved my life.

00:12:51.380 --> 00:12:53.680
I must thank you, young man.

00:12:55.820 --> 00:12:58.670
I am Baron Keyserling.

00:12:58.670 --> 00:13:03.340
Thank you for rescuing me, even
though we haven't met before.

00:13:04.400 --> 00:13:05.880
Keyserling ?

00:13:05.880 --> 00:13:08.800
He's retired
Rear Admiral Keyserling ?

00:13:09.900 --> 00:13:11.900
Thank you for
such kind words.

00:13:12.860 --> 00:13:16.710
I'm Imperial Fleet
Commander Siegfried Kircheis.

00:13:17.520 --> 00:13:20.180
Oh, you are young
for a Commander.

00:13:20.180 --> 00:13:22.480
Yes, I've been told that.

00:13:34.790 --> 00:13:38.500
Retired Rear Admiral
Michael von Keyserling.

00:13:39.250 --> 00:13:42.170
The present head of his family,
and a former Vice Admiral.

00:13:42.170 --> 00:13:47.070
He was held responsible for the
losses at Arlesheim 3 years ago.

00:13:47.070 --> 00:13:50.200
He was demoted to Rear Admiral
and was forced to retire.

00:13:51.480 --> 00:13:56.920
I've heard that the reason for the
defeat was his lack of leadership.

00:13:56.920 --> 00:14:02.190
But he doesn't look as incompetent
and undistinguished as has been said.

00:14:04.050 --> 00:14:06.970
Commander Siegfried Kircheis.

00:14:06.970 --> 00:14:11.320
I'm reluctant to trouble you...

00:14:11.320 --> 00:14:15.720
...but may I request that you please
accompany us to the police station ?

00:14:16.580 --> 00:14:18.200
Of course I will.

00:14:19.100 --> 00:14:20.650
Thank you for
your cooperation.

00:14:23.190 --> 00:14:25.850
Hello, red-haired,
tall guy there.

00:14:25.850 --> 00:14:26.930
You're strong.

00:14:26.930 --> 00:14:29.520
I should have bet
100 marks on you.

00:14:30.050 --> 00:14:32.030
I'm sorry to hear that.

00:14:32.580 --> 00:14:35.250
Oh well, I'm getting accustomed
to this sin city, aren't I ?

00:14:36.160 --> 00:14:37.320
Is anything troubling you ?

00:14:37.320 --> 00:14:39.020
No.  Let's go.

00:14:56.290 --> 00:14:59.610
You must be Commander Kircheis.

00:14:59.610 --> 00:15:01.170
I apologize for the trouble.

00:15:02.040 --> 00:15:06.070
I am the Chief Superintendent
of this town, Hoffmann.

00:15:08.320 --> 00:15:13.610
I very much appreciate that
you helped us out in this case.

00:15:14.610 --> 00:15:18.120
I was just there by chance.
You needn't thank me.

00:15:18.120 --> 00:15:20.830
Then I will have to
thank chance for this.

00:15:20.830 --> 00:15:23.120
By the way,
about that man...

00:15:23.120 --> 00:15:25.750
It's been reported that he was
under the influence of drugs.

00:15:25.750 --> 00:15:27.130
I knew it.

00:15:27.130 --> 00:15:28.130
You knew ?

00:15:28.130 --> 00:15:31.070
Well, it seemed like he
wasn't feeling any pain.

00:15:31.070 --> 00:15:33.230
It was quite bizarre.

00:15:33.230 --> 00:15:34.320
You're observant.

00:15:34.870 --> 00:15:40.860
In the last 50 years the use of a drug called Thyoxin has become prevalent in the Fleet and in rural areas.

00:15:41.270 --> 00:15:46.220
The man was liberated from the prison of 
reason by this drug and attacked that old man...

00:15:46.220 --> 00:15:49.540
...I mean, Baron Keyserling.

00:15:51.050 --> 00:15:55.070
Why are you telling me about this ?

00:15:55.070 --> 00:15:56.930
Such a thing must be kept
secret in an investigation.

00:15:58.200 --> 00:16:00.490
To tell you the truth...

00:16:00.490 --> 00:16:06.100
...when military personnel are involved in a crime,
there are times we can't operate as we like.

00:16:06.720 --> 00:16:08.020
Military personnel ?

00:16:08.020 --> 00:16:14.130
According to his ID the perpetrator is presently a chief petty officer, and yet an addict like that.

00:16:14.130 --> 00:16:19.740
Naturally, we suspect that the field that produces
drug addicts must be within his domain.

00:16:20.400 --> 00:16:23.720
If I understand you correctly, you believe
that the illegal distribution of the drug...

00:16:23.720 --> 00:16:26.470
...is done by an organization
within the military ?

00:16:28.120 --> 00:16:30.380
Yes, and
an organization.

00:16:30.380 --> 00:16:33.360
It couldn't be
done by an individual.

00:16:33.360 --> 00:16:39.580
Those who produce the drug, those who sell it,
those who distribute the profits, and so on.

00:16:39.580 --> 00:16:42.190
Their operation is very profitable.

00:16:42.190 --> 00:16:44.050
They're working for a common goal
and are committed to one another.

00:16:44.050 --> 00:16:46.670
They won't rat
each other out.

00:16:48.430 --> 00:16:50.160
What is he trying to tell me ?

00:16:50.160 --> 00:16:51.950
He's strangely theatrical.

00:16:53.190 --> 00:16:55.990
If they use a
route within the fleet...

00:16:55.990 --> 00:16:58.980
...it makes it especially difficult
for us to make an arrest.

00:16:58.980 --> 00:17:05.460
We hesitate to ask the cooperation of the Military Police unless there's a dire emergency of some sort.

00:17:06.630 --> 00:17:08.550
This is what the
military people say:

00:17:08.550 --> 00:17:11.860
"Leave matters involving military personnel to the Military Police."

00:17:11.860 --> 00:17:13.070
I see.

00:17:13.070 --> 00:17:16.670
You'd like me to cooperate with you on
your investigation of this drug organization.

00:17:17.520 --> 00:17:19.130
Yes. You seem
to understand.

00:17:19.130 --> 00:17:23.320
Superintendent Hoffmann,
I'm here on vacation.

00:17:23.320 --> 00:17:30.770
If I can, I'd like to leave my social
obligations in the attic for now and rest.

00:17:30.770 --> 00:17:32.420
Yes, I understand.

00:17:32.420 --> 00:17:39.040
It's unusual to make such a request and we're quite reluctant to...

00:17:39.040 --> 00:17:45.720
...but we've decided to launch
a full-frontal campaign.

00:17:48.120 --> 00:17:52.020
Are you telling me that I have
no right to refuse cooperation ?

00:17:52.020 --> 00:17:56.720
Of course you do, but I ask
you not to exercise your right.

00:17:56.720 --> 00:18:02.720
We're making this unreasonable request because we seem to have gotten a break in this case.

00:18:02.720 --> 00:18:03.720
A break ?

00:18:03.720 --> 00:18:10.720
The leader of the drug organization is
rumored to be arriving at Kreuznach III.

00:18:11.370 --> 00:18:15.720
Judging from what you say, I presume
you know who the leader is ?

00:18:16.370 --> 00:18:17.790
No, not at all.

00:18:17.790 --> 00:18:21.900
I understand you might laugh, but
we do have a reason for optimism.

00:18:21.900 --> 00:18:24.120
There has been
an anonymous tip.

00:18:24.120 --> 00:18:26.370
Of course, we're not naive.

00:18:26.370 --> 00:18:31.230
We've considered the possibility
that the tip might be a scheme...

00:18:31.230 --> 00:18:37.720
...to concentrate police
power on this satellite.

00:18:38.320 --> 00:18:41.720
That way, other places can't
be as closely monitored...

00:18:41.720 --> 00:18:46.550
...and they could launch
operations elsewhere.

00:18:47.790 --> 00:18:53.100
The leader of the Thyoxin drug organization
will soon pay a visit to Kreuznach III.

00:18:53.520 --> 00:18:54.730
Please believe me.

00:18:56.950 --> 00:18:58.470
Is that it ?

00:18:58.470 --> 00:19:00.700
That's it.{Yes, indeed.}

00:19:00.700 --> 00:19:04.100
In the end, you
decided to believe it.

00:19:04.810 --> 00:19:09.620
It's more like we have no
choice but to believe it.

00:19:10.720 --> 00:19:17.190
As you know, Thyoxin isn't a natural product;
it's chemically engineered in factories.

00:19:17.990 --> 00:19:22.880
The pleasure you get from it is unbelievable, but it's also highly poisonous.

00:19:22.880 --> 00:19:29.440
Its teratogenic and hallucinogenic capacities
definitely shouldn't be underestimated.

00:19:29.440 --> 00:19:30.910
Teratogenic ?

00:19:30.910 --> 00:19:35.970
It's the effect that the drug has on the
addict's offspring, not the addict himself.

00:19:35.970 --> 00:19:37.560
Seeing is believing.

00:19:37.560 --> 00:19:38.730
I'd like you
to watch this.

00:19:42.890 --> 00:19:47.120
The parents of this
child were both addicts.

00:19:47.120 --> 00:19:52.810
The father got addicted while in military
service, and brought the habit home.

00:19:52.810 --> 00:19:57.820
Afterwards, the mother killed herself, and
the father was sent to a mental hospital.

00:19:58.220 --> 00:20:03.060
Human folly must be
overlooked to some extent.

00:20:03.720 --> 00:20:07.520
Humans are like bread made of
the wheat flour called morality...

00:20:07.520 --> 00:20:09.920
...and the water
called desires.

00:20:10.770 --> 00:20:13.570
Bread with too much
flour will be too dry...

00:20:13.570 --> 00:20:17.410
...and bread with too much
water can't retain its shape.

00:20:17.410 --> 00:20:23.080
A leisure land like this little satellite exists
to supply enough water to dry bread.

00:20:23.650 --> 00:20:29.000
So we allow gambling, sex, alcohol, fights and whatnot, but we can't be lenient on drug trafficking.

00:20:29.000 --> 00:20:32.450
We have to crack down on it.

00:20:32.450 --> 00:20:36.770
A wisp of hay, like this anonymous
tip, is better than nothing.

00:20:36.770 --> 00:20:38.160
I understand.

00:20:38.160 --> 00:20:41.430
I will do anything I can to assist you.

00:20:42.030 --> 00:20:44.670
Oh, I appreciate that.

00:20:45.520 --> 00:20:47.000
That'll be a big help.

00:20:47.710 --> 00:20:50.980
It looks like I've fallen for
the Superintendent's scheme.

00:20:51.880 --> 00:20:54.230
But that's okay.

00:20:54.230 --> 00:20:57.010
It's probably more rewarding
than a purposeless vacation.

00:20:57.860 --> 00:21:03.390
To tell you the truth, I'm planning to retire
sometime next year, once this case is over.

00:21:04.220 --> 00:21:08.020
I have a son and daughter-in-law, and
three grandchildren on my home planet.

00:21:08.020 --> 00:21:11.380
I'll stay with them, play with my
grandchildren during the day...

00:21:11.380 --> 00:21:13.320
...and read my favorite
mystery stories at night.

00:21:13.320 --> 00:21:17.520
I'd like to spend the rest of my life
like that, until I go where my wife is.

00:21:17.520 --> 00:21:19.410
Do you like mystery stories ?

00:21:19.410 --> 00:21:20.320
Yes.

00:21:20.320 --> 00:21:21.180
Oh, hey...

00:21:21.180 --> 00:21:26.220
...have you read this book called
"The Nightmare of the Deserted Sea Route" ?

00:21:26.220 --> 00:21:27.950
No.

00:21:27.950 --> 00:21:30.100
It's a very good book.

00:21:30.100 --> 00:21:31.460
It's a collection
of short stories...

00:21:31.460 --> 00:21:35.020
...but it's the best book of the
century, in my humble opinion.

00:21:35.020 --> 00:21:36.680
You should read it too, Commander.

00:21:36.680 --> 00:21:38.770
It's an especially
good book for a vacation.

00:21:40.290 --> 00:21:41.120
Sure.

00:21:46.420 --> 00:21:48.830
This is hot chocolate.

00:21:59.870 --> 00:22:05.650
Besides, just as it's meaningful to expel
incompetent and complacent aristocrats...

00:22:05.650 --> 00:22:07.580
...from their positions of authority...

00:22:07.580 --> 00:22:13.170
...it must also be good for society
if I help ban such criminals...

00:22:13.170 --> 00:22:17.130
...who profit from this drug that harms society over multiple generations.

00:22:18.770 --> 00:22:24.150
In November of Imperial Year 486,
Space Year 795...

00:22:24.150 --> 00:22:29.320
...Siegfried Kircheis was to
spend an unwanted vacation...

00:22:29.320 --> 00:22:34.310
...at the resort on the
artificial satellite Kreuznach III.

00:22:34.310 --> 00:22:40.020
Also, without asking for it, he was
to become involved in a criminal case.

00:22:39.150 --> 00:22:42.400
To be continued

00:22:45.720 --> 00:22:50.370
[ Time to Mourn, Time to Celebrate ]

00:22:45.720 --> 00:22:50.370
Ending Theme

00:22:45.720 --> 00:22:50.370
Vocals: Ogura Kei

00:22:52.120 --> 00:22:56.750
Kircheis:

00:22:52.120 --> 00:22:56.750
Hironaka Masashi

00:22:52.670 --> 00:23:08.950
Even when I feel empty and want to throw away my life, to die...

00:22:58.160 --> 00:23:02.830
Hoffmann:

00:22:58.160 --> 00:23:02.830
Kamiyama Takuzou

00:23:03.660 --> 00:23:08.390
